{"requests": [
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "our react frontend talks to an ADK agent on cloud run via /run_sse. tokens stream in fine, but when the agent calls a tool the UI just sits there for 5-8 seconds with nothing on screen. I want a little 'searching inventory…' / 'checking order status' line that shows up during the function call and goes away when the result comes back. which events in the stream should I key off, and how do I keep the partial text from jumping around when a tool call lands mid-answer?"},
 {"kind": "fits", "text": "Ok so I've been going back and forth on this for two days and I need someone to just help me decide. Building a support-chat thing for an internal tool (Next.js, agent is ADK in Python behind a FastAPI wrapper). Demo is Thursday. Option A: keep my hand-rolled JSON endpoints + fetch + my own message list component. Option B: drop in one of the open-source chat UI kits (CopilotKit / assistant-ui / whatever's sane right now) and adapt the agent's event stream to it. Requirements: resume past conversations from a sidebar, human approval buttons before the agent issues a refund, and the stream must not blow up if the backend errors halfway through a reply. What would you pick and what does the wiring look like?"},
 {"kind": "elsewhere", "text": "chat page works locally but once deployed the streamed replies come out in one big chunk at the end instead of word by word. frontend code is identical. we're behind a Google Cloud HTTPS load balancer -> Cloud Run. what's buffering it?", "needs_instead": "Deployment and infrastructure troubleshooting: configuring the load balancer / Cloud Run / proxy settings (buffering, HTTP/2, timeouts, response headers) so server-sent events aren't buffered, not building the browser-side chat interface."}
]}
